@startuml
' Behavior 3 (new): recovery and reconciliation after a failure.
' Authored in Slice 2. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
' Store-local inventory and the master record are both projections of the per-source
' event log. The side that lost state rebuilds by replay from the authoritative log;
' a resync compares per-source sequence watermarks first to decide what is missing.
!include style.puml
title Components-and-Connectors view: behavior, recovery and reconciliation

skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 235

participant "Store Agent" as SA #93C47D
database "Store durable log\n(Outbox + local\nevent log)" as SLOG #8E7CC3
database "Store-Local\nInventory" as SLI #8E7CC3
participant "Communications\nFront-End" as CFE #F1C232
database "CFE event store" as CFEDB #8E7CC3
participant "Central Master\nInventory" as CMI #F1C232

== Master-inventory crash and rebuild (AV-3) ==
CMI -> CMI : process crashes
note over CFE, CFEDB : the CFE keeps accepting and persisting events\nwhile the master is down; stores keep publishing
CMI -> CFE : subscribe (resume)
CMI -> CFE : resync (per-source lastKnownSequence)
CFE --> CMI : watermarks per source\n(acceptedThrough, earliestRetained)
note over CMI, CFE : compare per-source watermarks to find the gap
CMI -> CFEDB : replay-from-sequence (read path, per source)
CFEDB --> CMI : missing events in source order
note over CMI : apply idempotently; the master record is\ncurrent again within 30 min, store operation\nnever stops (AV-3)

== Store node restart and rebuild (TEST-2) ==
SA -> SA : supervised restart\n(in-memory state lost)
note over SLOG : the Outbox and local event log are durable\nand survive the restart
SA -> SLOG : resync: read per-source watermarks
SLOG --> SA : last applied / last appended sequence
note over SA, SLOG : compare per-source watermarks to decide what to replay
SA -> SLOG : replay local event log
SLOG --> SA : events in source order
SA -> SLI : rebuild projection (idempotent)
SA -> CFE : resync, then replay unacknowledged Outbox events\nIEP / TLS 1.3 mutual certs [secure]
note over SA, CFE : backlog drains at up to 2,000 events/s per store\nwhile live sales continue (PERF-4); detection and\nrestored access are measured to within 1 s (TEST-2)

legend right
  Both inventory copies are projections of the per-source
  event log. The side that lost state compares per-source
  sequence watermarks, then replays from the authoritative
  log: the store's own durable log for the store, the CFE
  event store for the master. Replay is idempotent, so no
  event is lost or applied twice.
endlegend
@enduml
